 "notes": [
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "Main set-up: two UNOs, 'old style' wiring: D11 MOSI, D12 MISO, D13 SCK, programmer D10 to target RESET, 5V to 5V, GND to GND. The target is powered through the 5V wire; the USB cable goes to the programmer only.",
  "The 10 uF capacitor sits across programmer RESET (+, long leg) and GND on the breadboard: wire7 puts RESET on strip 1t, and the capacitor's negative leg is on strip 2t, which wire8 takes to programmer GND.2.",
  "The LEDs are the optional ArduinoISP feedback LEDs: heartbeat on D9, error on D8, programming on D7. Each runs from its pin through its LED (anode toward the pin) and a 220 ohm resistor (the value is assumed) to the ground strip 2t. The resistors are on the cathode side, because the manual's picture is not specific.",
  "Strip 2t has exactly five holes, used by capacitor negative, wire8 and the three resistors, so no separate ground rail is needed.",
  "Breadboard hole names follow the catalogue scheme '<column><bank>.<row>'; the exact columns are chosen by me because the manual's pictures give no hole positions.",
  "Alternative boards in the table (Mega, Leonardo, Due, MKR, Nano) are not built."
 ],
